      "valuation_insights": "### Costco Wholesale Corporation (COST) Fiscal 2026 Financial Summary\n\n- **Annual Total Revenue:** $303.154 billion [C:revenue2026]\n- **Revenue Growth:** 10.14% year-over-year [C:revgrowth2026]\n- **Operating Income:** $11.685 billion with a margin of 3.85% [C:operatingincome2026, C:operatingmargin2026]\n- **Net Income Attributable to Costco:** $9.226 billion [C:netincome2026]\n- **GAAP Diluted EPS:** $20.76 per share [C:dilutedeps2026]\n- **Return on Average Equity:** 28.40% [C:roaequity2026]\n- **Debt to Equity Ratio:** 0.172 (including current portion of long-term debt) [C:debttoequity2026]\n- **Free Cash Flow:** $9.382 billion [C:freecashflow2026]\n- **Latest Quarterly Net Sales:** $93.9 billion, increasing 11.2% vs prior year quarter [C:qrevenue2026]\n- **Latest Quarterly Diluted EPS:** $6.75 per share [C:qdilutedeps2026]\n- **Price to Earnings (P/E) Ratio:** Approximately 43.58 based on price $904.7 / EPS $20.76 [C:pe2026]\n\n#### Peer Operating Margins (Total Revenue Consistent Basis)\n- Walmart (WMT): 4.18% [C:wmtope2026]\n- Target (TGT): 4.88% [C:tgtope2026]\n- BJ's Wholesale (BJ): 3.81% [C:bjope2026]\n\nCostco’s operating margin at 3.85% trails Walmart and Target but aligns closely with BJ’s Wholesale. The 10.1% revenue growth is solid amid peers.\n\n**Note:** Revenue is reported from the contract sales tag, which is assumed to represent total revenue including membership fees; quarterly net sales figures are separately reported and slightly lower, consistent with Costco’s disclosures (release line 10 and 39).\n\n**Insight:** Despite a non-recurring tariff refund boosting EPS in Q4, Costco sustained healthy operating income growth alongside accelerating cash flow and an improved leverage position, underscoring strong operational discipline and shareholder value creation beyond headline revenue gains. [Press Release, line 20]",
